# public/data/ is deliberately NOT ignored, including the national concession
# layer produced by `npm run extract`.
#
# It was previously ignored on the grounds that 41 MB of derived geometry
# should be regenerated rather than committed. That made the deployed app
# broken by construction: the extract script reads Folium HTML that lives
# outside the repo, so no CI or Vercel build can ever produce these files, and
# the Concession Explorer 404s in production.
#
# The size argument does not hold either. The geometry is repetitive
# coordinate arrays that compress about 20x, so git stores the whole layer in
# roughly 2 MB of packed objects and Vercel serves it gzipped.
